<body>

<p>This table provides summary statistics for water quality measurements taken at streams in the National Parks of the National Capital Region Network. Statistical values are based on site visit averages and are grouped according to selected comparision. By using the "Compare by" control, you can determine what sort of comparison you wish to do, either grouping by year, month, or site.</p>
<p>Table outputs the following statistical measurements:
  <li><b>Minimum:</b> The lowest recorded value in the selected data.</li>
  <li><b>Q1:</b> 25th percentile; the value below which 25% of the data falls under.</li>
  <li><b>Mean:</b> The average of all the data values.</li>
  <li><b>Median:</b> 50th percentile; the central value in a dataset when sorted.</li>
  <li><b>Q3:</b> 75th percentile; the value below which 75% of the data falls under.</li>
  <li><b>Maximum:</b> The highest recorded value in the selected data. </li>
  <li><b>Standard Deviation:</b> Measure of the spread or variability of the data. A higher standard deviation indicates more variation from the mean, while a lower value suggests the data points are closer to the mean.</li>
  <li><b>Site Visits:</b> The total number of unique site visits.</li>
  <li><b>Total Measurements:</b> The total number of measurements for a given site. </li>
  <li><b>Missing Values:</b> The number of values not collected or reported. </li>

<h4>Downloads</h4>

<p>Table can be copied, printed, or downloaded as a CSV, Excel, or PDF.</p>


</body>
</html>